d to stumbling during basketball games but has progressed to difficulty walking in dimly lit rooms and tripping over small objects.","Teachers have observed that he sometimes walks with a wide-based stance and grabs desks or walls for support in hallways.","Parents report that he seems less confident in his movements and avoids activities like running or playing outside with friends.","Regarding daily routines, he struggles with climbing stairs and walking to the bus stop, particularly when carrying a backpack.","He reports a recent fall in the dark when walking from his room to the bathroom, which caused parental concern.","He avoids sports because he feels unstable but continues to participate in academic clubs at school.","Parents express concern that his mobility issues are progressing despite good pulmonary control."]},{"sid":41483,"type":"pmh","lines":["Active Problem List:","- Respiratory epithelial metaplasia (diagnosed 2020-01-15)","- Cystic fibrosis with pancreatic insufficiency (diagnosed in infancy)","- Chronic rhinosinusitis","- Bronchiectasis","- Malabsorption syndrome with fat-soluble vitamin deficiencies","- Growth failure","","He has a history of cystic fibrosis diagnosed in infancy, with frequent pulmonary infections requiring multiple hospitalizations.","His mother reports that he struggles to maintain weight despite a high-calorie diet, and he frequently appears fatigued."]},{"sid":41484,"type":"psh","lines":["- Functional endoscopic sinus surgery (FESS) - age 12","- Port-a-cath placement for intravenous access - age 9","- Tympanostomy tube placement - age 6"]},{"sid":41485,"type":"medications","lines":["He remains on chronic inhaled antibiotics as well as chest physiotherapy.","He has been prescribed vitamin supplements, he often forgets to take them, particularly when rushing to school.","","Home Medications:","- Pancrelipase (Creon) 36,000 lipase units with meals, 18,000 with snacks","- Vitamin E (alpha-tocopherol) 400 IU PO daily (variable adherence per patient report)","- Vitamin D3 (cholecalciferol) 2000 IU PO daily","- Vitamin A (retinol) 10,000 units PO daily","- Vitamin K (phytonadione) 2.5 mg PO daily","- Tobramycin inhalation solution 300 mg nebulized BID (28 days on, 28 days off)","- Dornase alfa (Pulmozyme) 2.5 mg inhaled daily via nebulizer","- Albuterol HFA inhaler 2 puffs inhaled Q4H PRN for bronchospasm","- Elexacaftor/Tezacaftor/Ivacaftor (Trikafta) 2 tablets PO q12h (morning and evening doses)","- Azithromycin 250 mg PO MWF (chronic suppressive therapy)"]},{"sid":41486,"type":"allergies","lines":["No known drug allergies, Iodine contrast (reaction: rash)"]},{"sid":41487,"type":"family_history","lines":["There is no family history of neurologic disorders."]},{"sid":41488,"type":"social_history","lines":["He has no history of alcohol or drug use.","His school performance remains normal, and he is mentally sharp.","He feels embarrassed by his clumsiness."]},{"sid":41489,"type":"ros","lines":["He denies headache, double vision, difficulty swallowing, or changes in bladder or bowel control.","He has not experienced depression."]},{"sid":41490,"type":"physical_exam","lines":["On examination, the boy appears thin, with a BMI at the 10th percentile for age.","His chest is hyperexpanded, with coarse crackles in the lung bases bilaterally.","His cardiac exam reveals a soft systolic flow murmur.","The abdomen is mildly distended but nontender, with no hepatosplenomegaly.","The extremities show no muscle wasting, but there is mild scoliosis.","Neurologic examination reveals an unsteady, wide-based gait.","Romberg test is positive, as he sways significantly when standing with his feet together and eyes closed.","Deep tendon reflexes are absent at the ankles.","Muscle strength is normal in the upper and lower extremities, but sensation testing shows decreased vibration and proprioception in the toes, while temperature and pain sensation are preserved.","Cranial nerves are intact, and coordination testing reveals dysmetria when performing heel-to-shin movements."]},{"sid":41491,"type":"labs","lines":["Laboratory studies are pending."]}],"orders":[]},{"id":10583,"date":"2022-07-15","type":"ed","dept":"Emergency Medicine","attending":"Dr. Jennifer Park","cc":"worsening shortness of breath, productive cough, and fatigue over the past week","order":2,"method":"template","question_ids":[4842],"sections":[{"sid":41492,"type":"chief_complaint","lines":["Worsening shortness of breath, productive cough, and fatigue over the past week"]},{"sid":41493,"type":"pmh","lines":["Active Problem List:","- Respiratory epithelial metaplasia (diagnosed 2020-01-15)","- Ataxia with vitamin E deficiency (diagnosed 2021-03-15)","- Cystic fibrosis with pancreatic insufficiency (diagnosed in infancy)","- Chronic rhinosinusitis","- Bronchiectasis","- Malabsorption syndrome with fat-soluble vitamin deficiencies","- Growth failure","","His parents report that he has had several hospitalizations in the past for lung infections and chronic sinusitis.","He has always been below the 5th percentile for height and weight and was diagnosed in infancy with meconium ileus requiring surgery.","Since early childhood, he has had frequent episodes of wheezing and foul-smelling, greasy stools that float in the toilet.","He uses a vibrating vest at home for chest physiotherapy and has had multiple courses of antibiotics in the past year."]},{"sid":41494,"type":"psh","lines":["- Functional endoscopic sinus surgery (FESS) - age 12","- Port-a-cath placement for intravenous access - age 9","- Tympanostomy tube placement - age 6"]},{"sid":41495,"type":"medications","lines":["He takes multiple oral medications, including pancreatic enzyme supplements and fat-soluble vitamins.","","Home Medications:","- Pancrelipase (Creon) 36,000 lipase units with meals, 18,000 with snacks","- Vitamin E (alpha-tocopherol) 400 IU PO daily (variable adherence per patient report)","- Vitamin D3 (cholecalciferol) 2000 IU PO daily","- 